  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>explore_retrieval - searches kb_chunks for each question in ../questions.csv and writes one row per match
with its score, no LLM.
Needs build_knowledge_base (lab 20) run first, Ollama with nomic-embed-text, the pcm-pgvector
container and a GENAI-EE license.

1. csvi-questions: CSV file input, ../questions.csv: question_id, question, expected_source.
2. emb-question: Text to Vector, Stream, Input Text Field question, Ollama nomic-embed-text at
   ${OLLAMA_URL}.
3. vs-matches: Vector Search, PGVector table kb_chunks, Max results ${TOP_K}, Min score ${MIN_SCORE},
   dimension 768, One row per match (rows without match kept), metadata source as match_source and
   chunk_index as match_chunk.
4. sv-matches: Select values, question_id, question, expected_source, match_rank, match_score,
   match_source, match_chunk.
5. txt-matches: Text file output, retrieval_matches.csv beside this file, fields at minimal width.

Run it with other TOP_K and MIN_SCORE values in Run Options to see what each keeps.</note>
      <xloc>160</xloc>
      <yloc>32</yloc>
      <width>623</width>
      <heigth>296</heigth>
      <fontname>Segoe UI</fontname>
      <fontsize>10</fontsize>
      <fontbold>N</fontbold>
      <fontitalic>N</fontitalic>
      <fontcolorred>0</fontcolorred>
      <fontcolorgreen>0</fontcolorgreen>
      <fontcolorblue>0</fontcolorblue>
      <backgroundcolorred>167</backgroundcolorred>
      <backgroundcolorgreen>224</backgroundcolorgreen>
      <backgroundcolorblue>245</backgroundcolorblue>
      <bordercolorred>100</bordercolorred>
      <bordercolorgreen>100</bordercolorgreen>
      <bordercolorblue>100</bordercolorblue>
      <drawshadow>Y</drawshadow>
    </notepad>
  </notepads>
